  "description": "The avatera system is a 4-arm teleoperated robotic platform developed by avateramedical GmbH for robot-assisted minimally invasive surgery. It comprises a single patient cart carrying four multi-joint robotic arms, a closed surgeon console with an immersive 3D stereoscopic viewer, and single-use 5 mm articulating instruments and single-use 3D endoscopes designed to eliminate sterile reprocessing. The system received European CE mark certification in 2019 for gynecological and urological procedures before the company ceased commercial operations.",
